You receive three inputs:
1) Receipt IMAGE
2) OCR TEXT draft
3) ITEMS_SOLD_COUNT (integer)

SOURCE OF TRUTH
- IMAGE and ITEMS_SOLD_COUNT are authoritative. OCR is only a hint.

OUTPUT (ABSOLUTE REQUIREMENT)
- Output ONLY a valid JSON ARRAY (start with "[" and end with "]").
- No prose, no markdown, no code fences, no headings, no extra whitespace outside JSON, no error objects.
- The array MUST contain exactly ITEMS_SOLD_COUNT objects.

JSON FORMAT
[
  {"Title":"<verbatim receipt line text>","Cost":0.00},
  ...
]

EXTRACTION RULES
- Include ONLY priced item lines (a line with a price on the right) from the IMAGE.
- EXCLUDE totals/summary lines even if priced: SUBTOTAL, TAX, TOTAL, TENDER, etc.
- EXCLUDE metadata: store/address/date/time/cashier/card/approval/change.
- ONE printed receipt line = ONE object. Never merge lines.
- Lines starting with “+” (e.g., “+CRV …”) must be their own objects if they have a price.
- Title: copy verbatim from the same line. No normalization or interpretation.
- Cost: copy ONLY the price from the same line. Strip trailing flags like F/T. Use a JSON number with two decimals.
  If receipt shows “.05”, output 0.05.

COUNT GUARANTEE (DO NOT FAIL)
- If you cannot confidently reach exactly ITEMS_SOLD_COUNT priced item lines, do NOT output anything except the best-effort JSON array with EXACTLY ITEMS_SOLD_COUNT objects by:
  - prioritizing clearly priced item lines first,
  - for any remaining required objects, use {"Title":"?","Cost":0.00} as placeholders.
- Never output error text or additional fields—JSON array only.
